<section id="floor-planning" class="sect planning" aria-labelledby="planning-title">
  <div class="sect-inner sect-split">
    <div class="planning-intro">
      <p class="t-kicker">Planning an Edmonton floor coating</p>
      <h2 id="planning-title" class="t-title" data-reveal="title">Before you choose a colour.</h2>
      <p class="t-body" data-reveal="fade">A useful floor starts with a useful conversation. Tell us what the space needs to do, what the concrete looks like now, and what you would like to change.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="planning-answers" data-reveal="fade">
      <details><summary><span class="planning-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><span>What condition is your concrete in?</span></summary><div class="planning-answer"><p>Dust, cracks, pitting and an existing coating are all worth mentioning before an Edmonton garage-floor assessment. Include photographs of the whole room and close-ups of the areas that concern you. The preparation discussion comes before the final finish recommendation.</p><a href="/services/concrete-solutions">Understand concrete preparation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="planning-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><span>How will you use the room?</span></summary><div class="planning-answer"><p>Parking through winter, working at a bench and setting up a basement fitness area call for different conversations. Talk through wet footwear, cleaning, traction, equipment and the look you want. A basement coating is not a substitute for addressing moisture or planning the rest of a renovation.</p><a href="/services/residential-epoxy-flooring">Explore garage and home floor coatings <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="planning-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><span>What helps Denis prepare your quote?</span></summary><div class="planning-answer"><p>Share your location, approximate floor area, current surface and preferred way to be contacted. Tell us about access, items that need moving and any schedule constraints. Preparation, repair and finish choices shape the scope; an attractive sample on screen is the start of the decision, not a final specification.</p><a href="/contact#quote">Tell Denis about your space <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="planning-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><span>Planning a shop or commercial floor?</span></summary><div class="planning-answer"><p>Start with the working day: traffic, cleaning routines, equipment, access and when the area can be taken out of use. Bring those details into the assessment so the conversation covers both the finished appearance and the practical installation plan.</p><a href="/services/commercial-epoxy-flooring">Discuss a commercial floor <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
